cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MORTIS: cohort-scale analysis for spatial metabolomics"
message: >-
  Please cite the software using the metadata below, including the version
  you actually ran. A Zenodo DOI will be added here shortly, and once the
  paper is out the preferred citation will be the article.
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-30"
license: MIT
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Faris
    family-names: Hrvat
    email: farishrvatit@gmail.com
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/FarisHrvat/mortis"
url: "https://farishrvat.github.io/mortis/"
abstract: >-
  A Python package for downstream analysis of spatial metabolomics data
  (MALDI-MSI, DESI and related imaging mass spectrometry). It tests at the
  patient level rather than the pixel level, measures differential spatial
  organization, whether a metabolite is arranged differently between groups
  independently of how much of it there is, compares cohorts and timepoints,
  and exports publication figures alongside a sealed manifest that lets a
  reviewer verify an analysis reproduces without access to the underlying data.
keywords:
  - spatial metabolomics
  - imaging mass spectrometry
  - MALDI-MSI
  - pseudobulk
  - spatial statistics
  - reproducibility
  - bioinformatics
  - anndata
identifiers:
